CM_ SG_ 312 HmiEngHybSts "Hmi Engine hybrid status operates when ECM determines that fuel is to old and informs driver. The bitcoding: Bit0 : Aged fuel, Fill up fuel tank. Bit1 : Aged fuel, Start petrol engine. Bit2 : Aged fuel, Engine will run to consume fuel. Bit3 : Aged fuel and low fuel level, Fill fuel. Bit4 : Spare";
CM_ SG_ 312 HmiFuLidNotClsd "HmiFuLidNotClsd: Hmi Fuel lid not closed is a warning and a message to the driver that the fuel lid is not closed. 0= No Warning. 1= Fuel Lid Not Closed Warning.";
CM_ SG_ 312 HmiFuLidOpenSts "HmiFuLidOpenSts: Hmi Fuel lid open status informs the driver with a DIM message that the system is venting the tank pressure and unlocking of the fuel tank lid is processing signal coding: 0 = unlocking not initiated, no status. 1= Please wait now opening";
CM_ SG_ 312 HmiFuTankRdy "HmiFuTankRdy: Hmi Fuel tank ready, informs the driver with a DIM message that the system is ready and it is possible to refuel. 0 = System is not ready. 1 = System is ready - Fuel can be filled. 2= Tank Lid can be open, but risk of splashing due to remaining pressure.";
CM_ SG_ 312 HmiVehStopForRefu "HmiVehStopForRefu: Fuel lid button pushed by mistake in vehiclespeed greater than 30km/h a message to the driver that the vehicle need to stop before preparing for refueling. 0= No Warning; 1= Please stop vehicle before refueling.";
