CM_ SG_ 880 TrsmCluTEstimdOfClu0 "Clutch C0 temperature";
CM_ SG_ 880 TrsmErrIndcnReq "TCM uses signal Transmission Error Indication Request to send a MIL-request to ECM. ECM will then act upon this request and iluminate the MIL. For VEP software, TCM transmits signal after two consecutive failed driving cycles (for a MIL-relevant code). Default value - 0 (Off)";
CM_ SG_ 880 TrsmHotSt "Transmission hot state. Indicate transmission is in hot state. 0 - Not in hot state, 1 - Hot state level 1, 2 - Hot state level 2.";
CM_ SG_ 880 TrsmShiftInhb "Transmission Shift Inhibit. Block shifting request signal sent from transmission supplier. 0 - shift inhibit not active, 1 - Shift inhibit active.";
